menu "Pinqeva firmware"

config PINQEVA_DEV_BYPASS_BOOTSTRAP
    bool "Disable factory bootstrap authentication (development only)"
    default n
    help
        Development-only escape hatch for boards that do not have a
        manufacturing-injected bootstrap key. When enabled, BLE connections
        are treated as authorized after pairing and the bootstrap HMAC is not
        checked. Never enable this for production hardware.

config PINQEVA_LOG_ADVERTISEMENT_KEY
    bool "Log advertisement-key bytes (development only)"
    depends on PINQEVA_DEV_BYPASS_BOOTSTRAP
    default n
    help
        Log the 28-byte advertisement key received over the encrypted BLE
        provisioning characteristic as uppercase hexadecimal. Advertisement
        keys are public protocol material, but logging them can expose device
        identity material. Keep this disabled for production hardware.

config PINQEVA_DEV_BYPASS_ENTITLEMENT
    bool "Advertise finder payload when an advertisement key exists (development only)"
    depends on PINQEVA_DEV_BYPASS_BOOTSTRAP
    default n
    help
        Development-only bypass for the signed-subscription entitlement. When
        enabled, a tag with a stored advertisement key immediately emits the
        Apple-style offline-finding manufacturer payload. This firmware does
        not verify an entitlement in this mode and must never be used on a
        production tag.

endmenu
